{"from": "claim:mk-03-06-herodians-conspiracy", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-12-14-pharisees-plotted", "note": "Matthew names only the Pharisees going out and conspiring to destroy Jesus; Mark adds that they conspired with the Herodians."}
{"from": "claim:mk-03-06-herodians-conspiracy", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-22-16-pharisees-herodians", "note": "The same Pharisee-Herodian coalition appears again at Matthew 22:16 (Mark 12:13)."}
{"from": "claim:mk-03-06-herodians-conspiracy", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-herodians"}
{"from": "claim:mk-03-08-crowds-from-idumea-tyre-sidon", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-04-25-crowds-followed", "note": "Matthew's crowd list (Galilee, Decapolis, Jerusalem, Judea, beyond the Jordan) omits Idumaea, Tyre and Sidon; Mark adds those three and omits Decapolis."}
{"from": "claim:mk-03-17-boanerges", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-language-of-jesus"}
{"from": "claim:mk-03-22-scribes-from-jerusalem-beelzebul", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-12-24-beelzebul-accusation", "note": "Matthew attributes the Beelzebul accusation to the Pharisees; Mark to scribes who came down from Jerusalem. The accusation itself is the same."}
{"from": "claim:mk-03-22-scribes-from-jerusalem-beelzebul", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-10-25-beelzebul", "note": "The same name \"Beelzebul\" for the ruler of demons is recorded at Matthew 10:25; its etymology is disputed there."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-13-idumaea", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikisource-ant13-idumaea"}
{"from": "site:maresha", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-maresha"}
{"from": "site:maresha", "type": "attests", "to": "place:idumaea", "grade": "B", "note": "Tel Maresha (Marissa), excavated in the Shephelah, was a major city of Idumea from the Persian through the Hellenistic period (Josephus: \"Dora and Marissa, cities of Idumea\"); its burial caves are a UNESCO World Heritage Site."}
{"from": "text:pliny-nh-5-idumaea", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:perseus-pliny-5-idumaea"}
{"from": "text:pliny-nh-5-idumaea", "type": "attests", "to": "place:idumaea", "grade": "A", "note": "Pliny names Idumaea as the region where “Idumæa and Palæstina begin” past the Sirbonian Lake - the same region, named, in the first century."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-13-idumaea", "type": "attests", "to": "place:idumaea", "grade": "A", "note": "Josephus names Idumea as a country with its cities (Dora, Marissa) and people; Hyrcanus conquered the Idumaeans and incorporated them into the Jewish state on condition of circumcision and the laws of the Jews, so Idumaea belonged to the Jewish world of the first century."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-13-idumaea", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-03-08-crowds-from-idumea-tyre-sidon", "grade": "C", "note": "Confirms the setting only: Idumaea was a real region inside the Jewish kingdom whose inhabitants were practicing Jews by the first century. It cannot attest that a crowd actually came from there. Regraded B to C by architect review: that the regions existed and were populated is context for the crowd; the places themselves are attested at A on their place nodes."}
{"from": "text:pliny-nh-5-tyre-sidon", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-03-08-crowds-from-idumea-tyre-sidon", "grade": "C", "note": "Confirms the setting only: Tyre and Sidon were great, populated cities of Phoenicia in the period. It cannot attest that crowds came from them to Jesus. Regraded B to C by architect review: that the regions existed and were populated is context for the crowd; the places themselves are attested at A on their place nodes."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-8-eleazar", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-03-11-unclean-spirits-son-of-god", "grade": "C", "note": "Exorcism of demoniacs by Jewish practitioners existed in the period (Eleazar before Vespasian). Context for the unclean spirits, not for their confession \"Son of God\"."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-8-eleazar", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-03-22-scribes-from-jerusalem-beelzebul", "grade": "C", "note": "Jewish exorcists were a reality in the period - the background of the accusation \"by the prince of the demons he casts out the demons\" (\"by whom do your children cast them out\")."}
{"from": "artifact:galilee-boat", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-03-09-boat-kept-near", "grade": "C", "note": "A 1st-century fishing boat from the lake: small boats stood just off the crowded shore. Context, not the event."}
